<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">

<title>Ergodic Literature Presentation</title>

<style>
:root{
    --primary:#0078d4;
    --secondary:#0f172a;
    --accent:#38bdf8;
    --bg:#f8fafc;
    --text:#1e293b;
}

*{
    margin:0;
    padding:0;
    box-sizing:border-box;
    font-family:'Segoe UI',sans-serif;
}

body{
    background:var(--bg);
    color:var(--text);
    display:flex;
    min-height:100vh;
    overflow:hidden;
}

/* Sidebar */

.sidebar{
    width:280px;
    background:var(--secondary);
    color:white;
    padding:25px;
    overflow-y:auto;
}

.sidebar h2{
    margin-bottom:20px;
    color:var(--accent);
}

.nav-item{
    padding:12px;
    margin:8px 0;
    border-radius:8px;
    cursor:pointer;
    transition:0.3s;
}

.nav-item:hover,
.nav-item.active{
    background:rgba(255,255,255,0.15);
}

.content{
    flex:1;
    display:flex;
    flex-direction:column;
}

/* Header */

.header{
    background:white;
    padding:15px 30px;
    display:flex;
    justify-content:space-between;
    align-items:center;
    box-shadow:0 2px 10px rgba(0,0,0,.1);
}

.controls{
    display:flex;
    gap:10px;
}

button{
    border:none;
    background:var(--primary);
    color:white;
    padding:10px 18px;
    border-radius:8px;
    cursor:pointer;
}

button:hover{
    opacity:.9;
}

/* Slides */

.slides-container{
    flex:1;
    position:relative;
    overflow:hidden;
}

.slide{
    position:absolute;
    inset:0;
    padding:50px;
    overflow-y:auto;
    opacity:0;
    transform:translateX(50px);
    transition:all .5s ease;
    pointer-events:none;
}

.slide.active{
    opacity:1;
    transform:translateX(0);
    pointer-events:all;
}

.slide h1{
    font-size:3rem;
    color:var(--primary);
    margin-bottom:25px;
}

.slide h2{
    margin-bottom:15px;
}

.slide p,
.slide li{
    font-size:1.15rem;
    line-height:1.8;
}

.slide img{
    max-width:100%;
    border-radius:12px;
    margin-top:20px;
    box-shadow:0 5px 20px rgba(0,0,0,.15);
}

.grid{
    display:grid;
    grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;
    gap:40px;
    align-items:center;
}

.video{
    width:100%;
    height:500px;
    border:none;
    border-radius:12px;
}

/* Notes */

.notes{
    margin-top:30px;
    padding:15px;
    border-left:5px solid var(--primary);
    background:#eef6ff;
}

.notes h3{
    margin-bottom:10px;
}

/* Footer */

.footer{
    background:white;
    padding:12px 24px;
    border-top:1px solid #ddd;
    display:flex;
    justify-content:space-between;
}

.progress-wrap{
    width:250px;
    background:#ddd;
    border-radius:20px;
    overflow:hidden;
}

.progress{
    height:10px;
    background:var(--primary);
    width:20%;
}

@media(max-width:900px){

.sidebar{
    display:none;
}

.grid{
    grid-template-columns:1fr;
}

.slide{
    padding:25px;
}

.slide h1{
    font-size:2rem;
}

.video{
    height:250px;
}
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<!-- Sidebar -->

<div class="sidebar">

<h2>Ergodic Literature</h2>

<div class="nav-item active" onclick="goToSlide(0)">
Introduction
</div>

<div class="nav-item" onclick="goToSlide(1)">
Definition
</div>

<div class="nav-item" onclick="goToSlide(2)">
Characteristics
</div>

<div class="nav-item" onclick="goToSlide(3)">
Examples
</div>

<div class="nav-item" onclick="goToSlide(4)">
Video
</div>

<div class="nav-item" onclick="goToSlide(5)">
Conclusion
</div>

</div>

<!-- Main Content -->

<div class="content">

<div class="header">
<h3>Ergodic Literature Presentation</h3>

<div class="controls">
<button onclick="prevSlide()">◀ Previous</button>
<button onclick="nextSlide()">Next ▶</button>
<button onclick="toggleFullscreen()">Fullscreen</button>
</div>
</div>

<div class="slides-container">

<!-- Slide 1 -->

<section class="slide active">
<h1>Ergodic Literature</h1>

<p>
A form of literature that requires non-trivial effort from the reader to traverse the text.
Readers actively participate rather than simply consuming information linearly.
</p>

<img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1512820790803-83ca734da794?w=1200"
alt="Books">

<div class="notes">
<h3>Speaker Notes</h3>
Discuss how ergodic literature changes the role of the reader from observer to participant.
</div>

</section>

<!-- Slide 2 -->

<section class="slide">
<h1>Definition</h1>

<div class="grid">

<div>
<p>
The concept was introduced by
<strong>Espen Aarseth</strong> in 1997 in
<em>Cybertext: Perspectives on Ergodic Literature</em>.
</p>

<br>

<ul>
<li>Ergon = Work</li>
<li>Hodos = Path</li>
<li>"Work Path"</li>
</ul>
</div>

<div>
<img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1507842217343-583bb7270b66?w=1200">
</div>

</div>

</section>

<!-- Slide 3 -->

<section class="slide">
<h1>Key Characteristics</h1>

<ul>
<li>Reader participation is necessary.</li>
<li>Multiple reading paths.</li>
<li>Non-linear structure.</li>
<li>Interactive or decision-based progression.</li>
<li>May include digital or physical navigation challenges.</li>
</ul>

<div class="notes">
<h3>Speaker Notes</h3>
Compare a traditional novel to a choose-your-own-adventure experience.
</div>

</section>

<!-- Slide 4 -->

<section class="slide">
<h1>Examples</h1>

<ul>
<li><strong>House of Leaves</strong> - Mark Z. Danielewski</li>
<li><strong>Hopscotch</strong> - Julio Cortázar</li>
<li>Choose Your Own Adventure books</li>
<li>Interactive fiction</li>
<li>Hypertext narratives</li>
<li>Narrative-driven video games</li>
</ul>

<img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1521587760476-6c12a4b040da?w=1200">

</section>

<!-- Slide 5 -->

<section class="slide">
<h1>Video Example</h1>

<p>
Replace the VIDEO_ID below with your preferred YouTube video.
</p>

<br>

<iframe
class="video"
src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/VIDEO_ID"
allowfullscreen>
</iframe>

<div class="notes">
<h3>Speaker Notes</h3>
Provide a demonstration of interactive storytelling or cybertext.
</div>

</section>

<!-- Slide 6 -->

<section class="slide">
<h1>Conclusion</h1>

<p>
Ergodic literature expands storytelling beyond traditional reading.
The reader becomes an active participant whose choices,
navigation, and effort shape the experience.
</p>

<br>

<h2>Key Takeaway</h2>

<p>
Meaning emerges not only from the text itself but from
the reader's interaction with it.
</p>

</section>

</div>

<div class="footer">

<div id="counter">
Slide 1 of 6
</div>

<div class="progress-wrap">
<div class="progress" id="progress"></div>
</div>

</div>

</div>

<script>

const slides =
document.querySelectorAll('.slide');

const navItems =
document.querySelectorAll('.nav-item');

let currentSlide = 0;

function showSlide(index){

slides.forEach(slide =>
slide.classList.remove('active'));

navItems.forEach(item =>
item.classList.remove('active'));

slides[index].classList.add('active');
navItems[index].classList.add('active');

document.getElementById("counter").innerHTML =
`Slide ${index+1} of ${slides.length}`;

document.getElementById("progress").style.width =
((index+1)/slides.length*100)+"%";
}

function nextSlide(){

if(currentSlide < slides.length-1){
currentSlide++;
showSlide(currentSlide);
}
}

function prevSlide(){

if(currentSlide > 0){
currentSlide--;
showSlide(currentSlide);
}
}

function goToSlide(index){

currentSlide=index;
showSlide(index);
}

document.addEventListener('keydown',e=>{

if(e.key==="ArrowRight") nextSlide();

if(e.key==="ArrowLeft") prevSlide();
});

function toggleFullscreen(){

if(!document.fullscreenElement){
document.documentElement.requestFullscreen();
}else{
document.exitFullscreen();
}
}

showSlide(0);

</script>

</body>
</html>
